1
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,820
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,260
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:54,397
That's right, he's the man with the
60 billion double dollars on his head.

4
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:58,397
They say he showed up in Dankentown
recently, made quite a mess, I hear.

5
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,920
Heh, so what happened?

6
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:03,060
The whole town got zapped.

7
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:06,000
Mountains of corpses all over Dankin.

8
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:10,420
The coffin maker got so rich, he
built himself a mansion of wood.

9
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,120
Guy sounds plain crazy.

10
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,160
He's more than crazy.

11
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:18,187
I think we'd be wise to
keep a safe distance.

12
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,047
Messing with Vash is
like dancing with death.

13
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,101
He leaves a trail of
destruction wherever he goes.

14
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:26,837
Women, children, he don't care.

15
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,440
He'll kill them all.

16
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,540
They call him the humanoid typhoon.

17
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,957
I don't

18
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:21,040
know.

19
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,040
I finally found you.

20
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:23,950
One night.

21
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,637
And just look at this place.

22
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,857
I didn't believe the rumors, but
this guy really is a typhoon.

23
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,764
Over half the town ain't
nothing but rubble now.

24
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:35,538
That's real shame, but the
Undertakers must be happy.

25
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,917
So how many did he get this time?

26
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,580
One hundred? Two hundred?

27
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,140
Actually, zero.

28
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:45,860
There's a whole lot of injuries,
but somehow no fatalities at all.

29
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,905
I guess we had a miracle here.

30
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:49,660
Without God's help.

31
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:51,196
So what was he like?

32
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:56,500
Well, he wore red, had earrings,
a giant man with short legs.

33
00:04:57,080 --> 00:05:00,315
I'm afraid I didn't get a
real good look at him myself.

34
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:01,881
Thanks, Sheriff.

35
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,318
Whatever you do, stay away from him.

36
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,260
For your own good. Red.

37
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:12,180
The area of Dankin is mostly demolished.

38
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,461
All residents go to your
designated shelter areas.

39
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,860
The next update will be 4.30 p .m.

40
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:21,140
Until then, please enjoy
our musical selection.

41
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,480
What do you have?

42
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:41,280
A banana sundae. Huh?

43
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,720
And I will have a Kaite
Milly foie with Ceylon tea.

44
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:49,850
Listen,

45
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:53,297
missus, I'm afraid you'd better order milk
with that or that gag ain't gonna work.

46
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:57,017
Yeah, cause if you did, we'd give you
all the milk you could possibly want.

47
00:05:57,100 --> 00:06:00,688
Although I hate to tell you,
but it wouldn't exactly be free.

48
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,120
But I didn't say milk, I said Ceylon-T.

49
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,230
Hey!

50
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:09,840
Oh, sorry.

51
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,574
You little bitch, you!

52
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:16,570
Oh!

53
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:18,377
The student's leg broke again.

54
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,857
You have a spare, don't you?

55
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,157
You should be more careful.

56
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,070
Yeah, I know.

57
00:06:22,153 --> 00:06:22,997
What the hell is she?

58
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,100
She's a monster.

59
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:29,397
By the way, mister, we heard that Vash the
Stampede showed up in Felgnarl recently.

60
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,197
Is there anything you can tell us?

61
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,420
What about Bash?

62
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:33,973
And why are you asking?

63
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,897
Don't tell me you two
innocent-looking things

64
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,757
are after that $60 billion
double-dollar reward.

65
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,760
Oh, not at all.

66
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:43,549
Yeah, actually, we're just
passing through here on business.

67
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,670
Business?

68
00:06:44,753 --> 00:06:46,515
Well, I didn't exactly see him myself.

69
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:50,352
As far as I could tell, he was
gone from the city by dawn.

70
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:53,317
Last I heard, he was
headed out to the east.

71
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,897
Can you tell me any more about him?

72
00:06:54,980 --> 00:07:00,637
Hmm well he stands about 12
fields tall and he wields

73
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:03,897
a huge weapon he's supposed
to have a mohawk and nerves

74
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:08,517
of steel apparently he's
got tons of henchmen and a

75
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,718
reputation is the worst
womanizer anyone's ever seen?

76
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:18,580
Womanizer I heard what he said huge
weapon and a mohawk that's our man all!

77
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:23,610
right.

78
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,523
Where is he?

79
00:07:24,606 --> 00:07:25,571
Where the hell did he go?

80
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:28,408
I don't care if you
have to dig up the whole

81
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,130
area.

82
00:07:31,213 --> 00:07:32,157
I want you to find him.

83
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,070
I don't believe it.

84
00:07:33,153 --> 00:07:34,157
That little coward couldn't be him.

85
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,070
I don't

86
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,517
see any point sticking around this place.

87
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,477
Let's just move on.

88
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:43,217
So you think you're big enough to give
me orders now, you little weasel, huh?

89
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,857
You saw what he was wearing?

90
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:45,770
You know

91
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,937
I know that it's him.

92
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:50,667
Find him no matter what or I'll
have to break your neck, okay?

93
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:01,217
I thought I was going to
suffocate a minute there.

94
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,480
It's fast, boy!

95
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,640
Hi there! Pardon me.

96
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,868
Thanks for nothing, fellas.

97
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:24,107
That was a pretty close one.

98
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:26,117
I almost bought the farm back there.

99
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,917
It's actually a miracle that
I got away with it this time.

100
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:29,830
I found him!

101
00:08:29,913 --> 00:08:30,743
Over there!

102
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:34,650
Perfect shot!

103
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:42,740
Well, he thinks he's funny.
Hunt him down. Right.

104
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,720
I'm getting hungry.

105
