They're persistent.

106
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:57,940
Ha ha ha!

107
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:00,217
I'm like a sitting duck over here.

108
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,360
I'm defenseless.

109
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,500
Oh, shit.

110
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:10,280
Now, stand real still.

111
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:13,097
You wouldn't want this
gun to go off, would you?

112
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,137
I found him.

113
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,749
He's right over here boss.

114
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,917
Uh, would you mind lowering
your gun like a good boy?

115
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,420
Forget it You don't like pain, do you?

116
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,980
I'm used to it. Well,

117
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,277
I feel sorry for your wife
and kids You'll make them cry

118
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:28,437
ain't got no kids and most
women find me pretty offensive.

119
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:31,260
So I'm single sounds
like a pretty lonely life

120
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,120
I'm telling you.

121
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:36,397
You have to die!

122
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:39,240
It would sure make us all happy if you do!

123
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,548
Sorry, I don't do requests.

124
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,340
Get down!

125
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:54,970
Boss!

126
00:09:55,053 --> 00:09:55,883
Help me!

127
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,760
That's good work. My compliments.

128
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:03,197
Attacking while your pal
is in the line of fire.

129
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,162
Don't you care about him at all?

130
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,500
We're not pals.

131
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:08,564
Our fate is our being partners.

132
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:12,114
The only possible way he can
be happy is when I'm happy.

133
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:13,554
That's just beautiful.

134
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,817
You can shoot me if that'd
make you feel better.

135
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:19,777
That is, if your big gun of
yours isn't just for show.

136
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:21,397
Actually, I can't stand blood.

137
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:24,097
Just the very side of it
makes me feel a little faint.

138
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,010
Fine, then.

139
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:29,652
How about we find out what happens when
you get to see your own blood, huh?

140
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:33,680
Now, it would make me real
happy if you go hold him down.

141
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:41,630
There, now.

142
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,626
Do you see how devoted he is?

143
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:49,374
Hey, couldn't you guys be
just a little bit more gentle?

144
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:54,460
Alright, let's get our precious
little cargo to the feds right away.

145
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:59,001
Yeah, we're gonna be filthy rich!

146
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:06,610
Women?

147
00:11:06,693 --> 00:11:08,072
Are they friends of his?

148
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:11,026
Well, are they gonna try
and steal our reward?

149
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,580
We're going in.

150
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,050
Right.

151
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:28,997
Now what do you want?

152
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,900
I'm very pleased to meet you.

153
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,160
My name is Meryl.

154
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:37,757
I'm Meryl Stryfe and I'm here representing
the Bernardelli Insurance Society.

155
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,252
And I'm Millie Thompson.

156
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:42,537
This is a small token of our goodwill.

157
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,320
Nice going, Meryl!

158
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:46,580
What are you doing?

159
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,260
Are you here with him?

160
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:51,820
Actually, not at all.

161
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:56,842
We were sent here by the Bernardelli
Insurance Society to investigate a report of -

162
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,640
I finally found you.

163
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,520
It's the 60 billion double
dollar big bounty. Mr.

164
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:08,480
Vash the Stampede. Huh?

165
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,397
Huh? Huh?

166
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,800
My name is Luce Ruth,

167
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:15,805
I'm a bounty hunter, and some
people know me as Constance Rifle.

168
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:17,610
Mr.

169
00:12:17,693 --> 00:12:20,917
Vash the Stampede, time you know that
I'm here for the price on your head.

170
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,830
What's that?

171
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:22,820
Well, Merrill?

172
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:23,902
This looks bad.

173
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,071
Uh, did I miss something?

174
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,330
Mr.

175
00:12:39,413 --> 00:12:42,004
Vash the Stampede, it's
a privilege to meet you.

176
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:46,097
Your face is starting to look like
it belongs on the double dollar.

177
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:48,717
You really can't blame me
for coming after you now,

178
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,918
since your head is worth 60 billion.

179
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,660
What do we do, Meryl?

180
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,507
I think it's pretty obvious.

181
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,300
We've gotta... stop them.

182
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,417
So, did you say your name was Ruth?

183
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,757
Uh, could you excuse me?

184
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:02,137
Well, I'm glad to see
you enjoy your work, Mr.

185
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:04,657
Ruth, but I'm afraid that
you're just a little bit late.

186
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:06,620
Please, listen to me! Me, late?

187
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:08,360
I don't reckon so.

188
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:11,510
You asshole!

189
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,577
What the hell do you
think you're aiming at?

190
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:16,257
Just a sixty billion double
dollar skull, that's all.

191
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:17,460
Don't be a moron!

192
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:20,917
You think the boss is Vash?

193
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,176
Where the hell did you get that idea?

194
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,499
I ain't fool enough to
listen to some lame henchman.

195
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,837
Sorry, joke's over and I ain't laughing.

196
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:30,391
Huh, this is just stupid.

197
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:31,895
Quit wasting my time.

198
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,077
Get the hell out of it!

199
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:33,990
Don't move.

200
00:13:34,073 --> 00:13:37,777
You're dressed in a red coat, you've
got earrings, and your legs are short.

201
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,240
I'm convinced you are Vash the Stampede.

202
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,892
You're out of your mind!

203
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:46,777
Vash is a blond-haired man in a red coat,
and he carries a great big handgun, okay?

204
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,800
No, he isn't.

205
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:52,195
Vash the Stampede is a giant man with
a really huge weapon and a mohawk!

206
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,953
That's awfully strange.

207
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,957
Yeah, the rumors don't match.

208
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,275
So what do we do now?

209
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,417
What do we do now?

210
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,737
We have no choice but to
believe what we've heard.

211
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:02,800
But Meryl...

212
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,020
You're all crazy!

213
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:07,360
I'm not Vash! Hey, boss! Look!

214
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:12,720
The Fenzel pays 60 billion double dollars
for Vash the Stampede, dead or alive.

215
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:14,937
So it's your choice, friend.

216
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,491
I'd be happy to kill you now, if you like.

217
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,180
So he's blonde.

218
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,500
Has a red coat, a big gun.

219
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,140
I get it.

220
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,477
You're trying to get the
jump on me, aren't you?

221
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,240
Vash the Stampede! What'd he say?

222
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:32,477
You even came up with
that stupid fake name!

223
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,390
Nice touch!

224
00:14:33,473 --> 00:14:34,303
Wait a minute.

225
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:37,022
He is definitely the real thing.

226
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,400
Let's get him!

227
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:40,740
Hmm. Well, I'll be.

228
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:43,472
So this is how he stayed alive this long.

229
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,960
Come on, shoot!

230
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:57,420
You bastard!

231
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,300
Don't push your luck!

232
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,960
I'm really scared.

233
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:12,097
The Humanoid typeset is on the loose.

234
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,480
What do we do, Meryl?

235
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,400
What do we do? Duh.

236
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,151
We run away, that's what.

237
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:20,304
I guess it is important
to stay alive, isn't it?

238
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:25,937
We'll have to get the town the
evacuation order immediately.

239
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:30,557
But Meryl, isn't running away like this
the same as if we were abandoning our post?

240
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,057
It's more important that
we contact the town now.

241
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,728
Mmm, these are really good!

242
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:36,994
When did you get here?

243
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:37,970
Thanks a lot!

244
00:15:38,053 --> 00:15:39,097
I'm really getting hungry!

245
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:40,337
These donuts hit the spot!

246
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,960
Give me those!

247
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:45,946
You know, we didn't come out here
just to save your sorry butt!

248
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:48,397
Okay, then, what were you two doing there?

249
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,557
Are ugly donuts like that?

250
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:50,617
You're tight for what?

251
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,530
Shut up!

252
00:15:51,613 --> 00:15:52,517
It's not like that at all!

253
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,537
We came to this place
on official business!

254
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,450
That's right!

255
00:15:55,533 --> 00:15:57,777
Official representatives of the
Bernard Daly Insurance Society!

256
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:59,417
We're disaster investigators!

257
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,837
So, if you're really insurance people,

258
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,357
Why are you so interested
in such a dangerous bounty?

259
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:06,277
There's been over 300 incidents
involving Bash the Stampede.

260
